;; Guest scanout-bind decision: how many virtio-gpu scanouts to attach.
;;
;; WHY THIS IS A KOTOBA OBJECT AND NOT A C TABLE
;;
;; C already CREATE/ATTACH/XFER/FLUSH 2D resources and issues SET_SCANOUT
;; (mechanism). HOW MANY enabled modes become bound scanouts is a
;; compositor decision. ADR-0094 greened two resources on scanout 0.
;; Hosted `kbb -M:compositor wm` does not count as guest scanout-two.
;; The named leftover after this object is linked is still
;; `:native-compositor-absent` (native component runtime, P5).
;;
;; ABI: [n-resources n-enabled] → scanouts to bind, or 0 refuse.
;; Vector:
;;   (1, 2) → 0   one resource cannot occupy two scanouts
;;   (2, 1) → 0   one enabled mode is leftover :one-scanout
;;   (2, 2) → 2   two resources and two enabled modes
;; Returning 1 when both sides admit two is leftover :one-scanout.
;; Extra enabled modes still bind two (we have two resources).
;;
;; Temporary native constraint: word types only, nested `if`, not a map
;; (ADR-2608650000: an unavailable backend is not a language ceiling).
;; Param names match ime-romaji (`a` `b`). JVM loads `elf64.clj` over
;; `elf64.cljc`; the allow-list row must exist in the .clj file.
;;
;; Not a second compositor west repo. Not hosted JVM WM.

(defn aiueos-scanout-bind [a b]
  (if (< a 2) 0
    (if (< b 2) 0
      2)))

(defn main [] 0)
